  "_comment": "Maps every vanilla Vintage Story 1.22.7 food to USDA FoodData Central (SR Legacy, April 2018) entries. Read by tools/build_food_profiles.py. 'grams' is the real weight of one in-game item (grams per litre for liquids). 'fdc' is a list of FDC ids averaged with equal weight. 'water' rescales the profile to that water content (dry-matter scaling, used for breads, doughs and dried foods). 'zero' sets nutrients to 0 (for example vitamin C lost in baking). 'juice' removes fiber (pulp pressed out). 'slicesOf'/'slices' sizes a cheese wheel from its single slice. 'factor' is a gameplay multiplier on top of the USDA values (one number for every nutrient, or a {nutrient: multiplier} map); 'stateFactors' does the same for a state named in the item code and scales every nutrient for items whose code contains that state (part-baked bread keeps 50%, charred 20%). 'fallback' leaves the item on its vanilla category template because USDA has no suitable entry.",
  "_fallbackComment": "Only foods with no profile (insects, other mods' foods) are sized from vanilla satiety, at fallbackKcalPerSatiety kcal per satiety point, because nothing else is known about them.",
